# macOS shadcn components

Controls should read as current macOS (Tahoe / Liquid Glass) — context decides fill.

## Inputs / selects / textarea

| Class | When | Look |
|-------|------|------|
| `.macos-input` (default Input/Textarea) | Boxed entry (time fields, compact fields) | Subtle grey well + soft `0.5px` border + ~6px radius |
| `.macos-input-plain` | Stacked label forms (Request) | Transparent, no border |
| `.macos-select` | Settings row values | Text + `ChevronsUpDown` only, no well |
| `.macos-search` | Finder / Settings / Safari search | Capsule fill, no hard border |

- Focus on boxed fields: accent ring via `color-mix(... var(--macos-accent) ...)`
- Never hardcode `#007aff` — use `var(--macos-accent)`

## Switch & radio

- Switch: accent on, flat `#e5e5ea` off, white thumb
- Radio: flat grey off; accent + white center dot on

## Floating chrome (Tahoe) — two patterns

- Toolbar actions: `FloatingGroup` / `FloatingGroupButton`
- **Settings-style:** `FloatingSidebar` (+ Shell/Content) — **sidebar floats**, content flush
- **Finder-style:** flush dark chrome + sidebar; **`FloatingContent`** inset card floats (top toolbar stays on chrome; search often plain/`macos-input-plain`)
- Don’t mix both floating surfaces in one window
